<article class="env-lemma" id="0AYS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AYS">Lemma <span data-tag="0AYS">33.44.3</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper scheme of dimension $\leq 1$ over $k$. Let $0 \to \mathcal{E}_1 \to \mathcal{E}_2 \to \mathcal{E}_3 \to 0$ be a short exact sequence of locally free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules each of finite constant rank. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \deg (\mathcal{E}_2) = \deg (\mathcal{E}_1) + \deg (\mathcal{E}_3)  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from additivity of Euler characteristics (Lemma <a href="/tag/08AA" data-tag="08AA">33.33.2</a>) and additivity of ranks. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>